== Chapter II

#block(inset: (x: 1em))[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #text(size: 0.9em)[#emph[The principal Assertion concerning the Necessity of Mortification proposed to Confirmation. Mortification the Duty of the best Believers,] Col 3:5. 1 Cor 9:27. #emph[Indwelling Sin always abides: No Perfection in this Life.] Phil 3:12. 1 Cor 13:12. 2 Pet 3:18. Gal 5:17 etc. #emph[The Activity of abiding sin in Believers:] Rom 7:23. Jas 4:5. Heb 12:1. #emph[Its Fruitfulness and Tendency. Every Lust aims at the height in its kind. The Spirit and new Nature given to contend against Indwelling Sin.] Gal 5:17. 2 Pet 1:4, 5. Rom 7:23. #emph[The fearful Issue of the Neglect of Mortification.] Rev 3:2. Heb 3:13. #emph[The first general Principle of the whole Discourse hence confirmed. Want of this Duty lamented.]]
]

#smallcaps[Having] laid this Foundation, a brief Confirmation of the forementioned principal #emph[Deductions] will lead me to what I chiefly intend. The first is,

That #emph[The choicest believers, who are assuredly freed from the condemning power of Sin, ought yet to make it their business all their days to mortify the Indwelling power of Sin.]

So the Apostle, Col 3:5. #emph[Mortify therefore your members, which are upon the earth.] Whom speaks he to? Such as were #emph[risen with Christ,] v. 1 such as were #emph[dead with him,] v. 3 such as whose Life Christ was, and who should #emph[appear] with him in #emph[Glory,] v. 4. #emph[Do you mortify]\; do you make it your daily work, be always at it whilst you live, cease not a day from this work; be killing Sin, or it will be killing you; your being #emph[dead] with #emph[Christ virtually,] your being #emph[quickened] with him, will not excuse you from this work. And our Savior tells us, how his Father deals with every #emph[branch in him that beareth fruit,] every true and living Branch; #emph[He purgeth] it, that it may bring forth #emph[more fruit,] John 15:2. He prunes it, and that not for a day or two, but whilst it is a #emph[branch] in this world. And the Apostle tells you what was his practice, 1 Cor 9:27. #emph[I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection.] I do it (saith he) daily, it is the work of my Life, I omit it not; this is my Business. And if this were the work and business of #emph[Paul,] who was so incomparably exalted in Grace, Light, Revelations, Enjoyments, Privileges, Consolations, above the ordinary measure of Believers; where may we possibly bottom an Exemption from this Work and Duty whilst we are in this world. Some brief account of the Reasons hereof may be given.

1\. #emph[Indwelling sin] always #emph[abides,] whilst we are in this world, therefore it is always to be #emph[mortified.] The #emph[vain,] foolish, and ignorant disputes of men, about #emph[perfect] keeping of the #emph[Commands] of God, of #emph[perfection] in this Life, of being #emph[wholly and perfectly dead] to sin, I meddle not now with. It is more than #emph[probable,] that the men of those Abominations, never knew what belonged to the #emph[keeping] of any one of Gods Commands; and are so much below #emph[perfection] of #emph[degrees,] that they never attained to a #emph[perfection] of #emph[parts] in Obedience, or #emph[universal] Obedience in sincerity. And therefore many in our days who have talked of #emph[perfection,] have been wiser, and have affirmed it to consist in knowing no difference between #emph[good and evil.] Not that they are perfect in the things we call #emph[good,] but that all is alike to them; and the height of Wickedness is their Perfection. Others who have found out a new way to it, by denying #emph[original] indwelling Sin, and attempering the #emph[spirituality] of the Law of God, unto men's carnal Hearts; as they have sufficiently discovered themselves to be ignorant of the Life of Christ, and the power of it in Believers, so they have invented a new Righteousness, that the Gospel knows not of, being vainly puffed up by their fleshly minds. For us, who dare #emph[not be wise above what is written,] nor #emph[boast] by other men's lines of what God hath not done for us, we say, that #emph[Indwelling Sin] lives in us in some measure and degree whilst we are in this world. We dare not speak as #emph[though we had already attained, or were already perfect,] Phil 3:12 our #emph[inward man is to be renewed day by day,] whilst here we live, 2 Cor 4:16 and according to the #emph[Renovations of the new,] are the breaches and decays of the #emph[old.] Whilst we are here, we #emph[know but in part,] 1 Cor 13:12 having a remaining darkness to be gradually removed, by our #emph[growth in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.] 2 Pet 3:18. And the Flesh lusteth against the Spirit, so that we cannot do the things that we would, Gal 5:17 and are therefore defective in our Obedience as well as in our Light, 1 John 1:8. We have a #emph[body of death,] Rom 7:24 from whence we are not delivered, but by the #emph[death of our bodies,] Phil 3:21. Now it being our Duty to mortify, to be killing of Sin whilst it is in us, we must be at work. He that is appointed to kill an Enemy, if he leave striking, before the other ceases living, doth but half his work. Gal 6:9. Heb 12:1. 2 Cor 7:1.

2\. Sin doth not only still #emph[abide] in us, but is still acting, still laboring to bring forth the deeds of the Flesh; When sin lets us alone, we may let Sin alone: But as Sin is never less quiet, than when it seems to be most quiet; and its waters are for the most part deep, when they are still; so ought our contrivances against it to be; vigorous at all times, in all conditions, even where there is least suspicion. Sin doth not only abide in us, but the Law of the #emph[members is still rebelling against the Law of the Mind,] Rom 7:23 and the Spirit that dwells in us lusteth to Envy, Jas 4:5. It is always in continual work, the #emph[flesh lusteth against the Spirit,] Gal 5:17. Lust is still #emph[tempting] and #emph[conceiving] sin, Jas 1:14. In every Moral Action, it is always either inclining to evil, or hindering from that which is good, or disframing the Spirit from Communion with God. It #emph[inclines] to Evil; #emph[the evil that I would not, that I do,] saith the Apostle, Rom 7:19 whence is that? Why because in me, #emph[that is, in my flesh dwelleth no good thing]: and it hinders from good; #emph[the good that I would do, that I do not,] v. 19 upon the same account, either I do it not; or not as I should; all my Holy things being defiled by this sin. #emph[The flesh lusteth against the Spirit, that ye cannot do the things that ye would,] Gal 5:17 and it unframes our Spirit; and thence is called the sin that so #emph[easily besets us,] Heb 12:1 on which account are those grievous Complaints that the Apostle makes of it Rom 7. So that sin is always acting, always conceiving, always seducing and tempting. Who can say that he had ever any thing to do with God, or for God, that #emph[indwelling] Sin had not an hand in the corrupting of what he did. And this trade will it drive more or less all our days; If then sin will be always Acting, if we be not always Mortifying, we are lost Creatures. He that stands still, and suffers his Enemies to double blows upon him without resistance, will undoubtedly be conquered in the issue: If Sin be subtle, watchful, strong, and always at work in the business of killing our Souls, and we be slothful, negligent, foolish, in proceeding to the ruin thereof, can we expect a comfortable Event? There is not a day but sin foils, or is foiled; prevails, or is prevailed on; and it will be so whilst we live in this world. I shall discharge #emph[him] from this Duty, who can bring sin to a Composition, to a #emph[cessation] of Arms in this Warfare; if it will spare him any one day, in any one duty, (provided he be a person that is acquainted with the #emph[spirituality] of Obedience, and the subtlety of sin) let him say to his Soul, as to this Duty, Soul take thy rest. The Saints whose Souls breathe after deliverance from its perplexing Rebellion, know there is no safety against it, but in a constant Warfare.

3\. Sin will not only be #emph[striving, acting, rebelling, troubling, disquieting,] but if let alone, if not continually #emph[mortified,] it will bring forth #emph[great, cursed, scandalous,] Soul-destroying sins. The Apostle tells us what the works and fruits of it are, Gal 5:19, 20, 21. #emph[The works of the flesh are manifest; which are, Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness, idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies, envyings, murders, drunkenness, revelings, and such like.] You know what it did in #emph[David,] and sundry others. Sin aims always at the utmost: every time it rises up to tempt or entice, might it have its own course, it would go out to the utmost sin in that kind. Every unclean Thought or Glance would be Adultery, if it could; every covetous Desire would be Oppression; every thought of Unbelief would be Atheism, might it grow to its head. Men may come to that, that sin may not be heard speaking a scandalous word in their hearts; that is, #emph[provoking] to any #emph[great] sin with scandal in its mouth; but every rise of Lust, might it have its course, would come to the height of Villany. It is like the Grave, that is never satisfied. And herein lies no small share of the #emph[deceitfulness] of Sin, by which it prevails to the hardening of men, and so to their ruin: Heb 3:13. It is modest as it were in its first #emph[motions] and Proposals; but having once got footing in the heart by them, it constantly makes good its ground, and presseth on to some farther degrees in the same kind; This new acting and #emph[pressing] forward, makes the Soul take little notice of what an entrance to a #emph[falling] off from God is already made; it thinks all is indifferent well, if there be no farther #emph[progress]\; and so far as the Soul is made insensible of any sin, that is, as to such a sense as the Gospel requireth, so far it is hardened: but Sin is still pressing forward; and that because it hath #emph[no bounds] but utter Relinquishment of God, and opposition to him; that it proceeds towards its #emph[height] by degrees, making good the ground it hath got by Hardness, is not from its #emph[Nature,] but its #emph[Deceitfulness.] Now nothing can prevent this, but #emph[Mortification.] That withers the Root and strikes at the Head of Sin every Hour, that whatever it aims at, it is crossed in. There is not the best Saint in the #emph[world,] but if he should give over this #emph[Duty] would fall into as many cursed sins as ever any did of his kind.

4\. This is one main reason why the Spirit and the new Nature is given unto us, that we may have a Principle within, whereby to oppose Sin and Lust: #emph[The Flesh lusteth against the Spirit:] Well, and what then? Why #emph[the Spirit also lusteth against the Flesh,] Gal 5:17. There is a propensity in the #emph[Spirit,] or spiritual new Nature, to be acting against the Flesh, as well as in the Flesh to be acting against the #emph[Spirit:] So 2 Pet 1:4, 5. It is our #emph[participation of the Divine Nature,] that gives us an #emph[escape from the pollutions that are in the world through lust:] and Rom 7:23 there is a #emph[law of the mind,] as well as a #emph[law of the members.] Now this is, (1) The most Unjust and unreasonable thing in the world; when two Combatants are engaged, to bind one, and to keep him up from doing his utmost, and to leave the other at liberty to wound him at his pleasure. And, (2) The Foolishest thing in the world, to bind him who fights for our Eternal Condition, and to let him alone who seeks and violently attempts our everlasting ruin. The Contest is for our #emph[lives] and #emph[souls.] Not to be daily employing the #emph[Spirit] and #emph[New Nature,] for the #emph[Mortifying] of Sin, is to neglect that #emph[excellent succor,] which God hath given us against our greatest Enemy. If we neglect to make use of what we have received, God may justly hold his hand from giving us more. His #emph[Graces] as well as his #emph[Gifts] are bestowed on us to use, exercise, and trade with. Not to be daily #emph[mortifying] sin, is to sin against the #emph[Goodness, Kindness, Wisdom, Grace,] and #emph[Love] of God, who hath furnished us with a Principle of doing it.

5\. Negligence in this Duty casts the Soul into a perfect contrary Condition to that, which the Apostle affirms was his, 2 Cor 4:16 #emph[Though our outward man perish, our inward man is renewed day by day.] In these the Inward man perisheth, and the Outward man is renewed day by day. Sin is as the #emph[house of David,] and #emph[Grace] as the #emph[house of Saul. Exercise] and #emph[success] are the two main #emph[cherishers] of Grace in the heart; When it is suffered to lie still, it withers and decays; the things of it are ready to die, Rev 3:2 and Sin gets ground towards the #emph[hardening of the heart;] Heb 3:13. This is that which I intend; by the Omission of this duty, Grace withers, Lust flourisheth, and the Frame of the Heart grows worse and worse: and the Lord knows what desperate and fearful issues it hath had with many. Where Sin through the Neglect of Mortification gets a considerable Victory, it breaks the bones of the Soul, Ps 31:10. Ps 51:8 and makes a man weak, sick, and ready to #emph[die,] Ps 38:3, 4, 5 that he cannot look up, Ps 40:12. Isa 33:24 and when poor Creatures will take blow after blow, wound after wound, foil after foil, and never rouse up themselves to a vigorous Opposition, can they expect any thing but to be hardened through the #emph[deceitfulness of sin]\; and that their Souls should bleed to death, 2 John 8? Indeed it is a sad thing to consider the fearful #emph[issues] of this Neglect, which lie under our eyes every day. See we not those whom we knew #emph[humble,] melting, broken-hearted Christians, tender and fearful to offend, zealous for God, and all his ways, his Sabbaths, and Ordinances, grown, through a neglect of watching unto this Duty, #emph[earthly,] carnal, cold, wrathful, complying with the men of the world, and things of the World, to the Scandal of Religion, and the fearful Temptation of them that know them? The truth is, what between placing #emph[mortification] in a rigid stubborn Frame of Spirit, which is for the most part earthly, legal, censorious, partial, consistent with Wrath, Envy, Malice, Pride, on the one hand, and pretenses of Liberty, Grace, and I know not what on the other, true #emph[Evangelical] Mortification is almost lost amongst us, of which afterwards.

6\. It is our Duty to be Perfecting Holiness in the #emph[fear of the Lord,] 2 Cor 7:1. To be growing in Grace every day, 1 Pet 2:2. 2 Pet 3:18. To be renewing our inward man day by day, 2 Cor 4:16. Now this cannot be done without the daily #emph[Mortifying] of sin: Sin sets its strength against every Act of Holiness, and against every degree we grow to. Let not that man think he makes any Progress in Holiness, who walks not over the bellies of his Lusts; He, who doth not kill Sin in his way, takes no steps towards his Journeys End. He who finds not #emph[opposition] from it, and who sets not himself in every particular to its #emph[Mortification,] is at #emph[peace] with it, not #emph[dying] to it.

This then is the first #emph[General] Principle of our ensuing Discourse: Notwithstanding the #emph[meritorious Mortification] (if I may so speak) of all and every Sin in the Cross of Christ; notwithstanding the real Foundation of universal Mortification laid in our first Conversion, by Conviction of Sin, #emph[humiliation] for sin, and the Implantation of a new Principle, opposite to it, and #emph[destructive] of it; yet Sin doth so remain, so act, and work, in the best of Believers, whilst they live in this world, that the #emph[constant daily Mortification] of it is all their days #emph[incumbent] on them. Before I proceed to the Consideration of the next Principle, I cannot but by the way #emph[complain] of many #emph[Professors] of these days; who instead of bringing forth such great and evident Fruits of #emph[Mortification,] as are expected, scarce bear any Leaves of it. There is indeed a broad Light fallen upon the men of this Generation; and together therewith many #emph[spiritual Gifts communicated]\; which with some other Considerations have wonderfully enlarged the bounds of Professors and Profession; both they and it are exceedingly multiplied and increased. Hence there is a noise of Religion and Religious Duties in every corner; preaching in abundance; and that not in an empty, light, trivial and vain manner, as formerly, but to a good proportion of a spiritual Gift; so that if you will measure the number of #emph[Believers] by Light, Gifts and profession, the Church may have cause to say, #emph[Who hath born me all these?] But now if you will take the measure of them by this great discriminating Grace of Christians, perhaps you will find their number not so multiplied. Where almost is that Professor, who owes his #emph[Conversion] to these days of Light, and so talks and professes at such a rate of Spirituality, as few in former days were in any measure acquainted with, (I will not judge them, but perhaps #emph[boasting] what the Lord hath done in them) that doth not give evidence of a miserably unmortified heart? If vain #emph[spending of Time, idleness, unprofitableness] in men's places, #emph[envy, strife, variance, emulations, wrath, pride, worldliness, selfishness,] (1 Cor 1) be Badges of Christians, we have them on us and amongst us in abundance. And if it be so with them who have much #emph[Light,] and which we hope is #emph[saving]\; what shall we say of some who would be accounted #emph[religious,] and yet despise Gospel Light, and for the Duty we have in hand, know no more of it, but what consists in men's Denying themselves sometimes in outward Enjoyments, which is one of the outmost Branches of it, which yet they will seldom practise! The good Lord send out a spirit of #emph[Mortification] to cure our Distempers, or we are in a sad Condition.

There are two Evils which certainly attend every #emph[unmortified] Professor. The first in himself, the other in respect of others.

1\. In #emph[himself,] let him pretend what he will, he hath #emph[slight thoughts of Sin]\; at least of sins of daily infirmity. The Root of an unmortified Course, is the #emph[digestion] of Sin, without bitterness in the heart; When a man hath confirmed his Imagination to such an Apprehension of #emph[Grace] and #emph[Mercy,] as to be able without bitterness to swallow and digest daily sins, that man is at the very brink of #emph[turning the Grace of God into lasciviousness,] and being #emph[hardened by the deceitfulness of Sin.] Neither is there a greater Evidence of a #emph[false] and rotten heart in the world, than to drive such a Trade. To use the #emph[blood of Christ,] which is #emph[given to cleanse us,] 1 John 1:7. Titus 2:14. The #emph[exaltation] of Christ, which is to give us #emph[Repentance,] Acts 5:31 the #emph[Doctrine of Grace,] which teaches us to #emph[deny all ungodliness,] Titus 2:11, 12 to countenance Sin, is a Rebellion, that in the issue will break the #emph[bones.] At this door have gone out from us, most of the professors that have #emph[Apostatized] in the days wherein we live, for a while they were most of them under Convictions; these kept them unto Duties, and brought them to Profession. So they #emph[escaped the pollutions that are in the world, through the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ,] 2 Pet 2:20. But having got an acquaintance with the Doctrine of the Gospel, and being weary of Duty, for which they had no Principle, they began to countenance themselves in manifold Neglects, from the Doctrine of Grace. Now when once this evil had laid hold of them, they speedily tumbled into perdition.

2\. To #emph[others,] it hath an evil Influence on them, on a twofold account.

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. It #emph[hardens] them, by begetting in them a Persuasion that they are in as good Condition as the #emph[best] Professors. Whatever they see in them, is so stained for want of this Mortification, that it is of no value with them: They have Zeal for Religion, but it is #emph[accompanied] with #emph[want] of #emph[forbearance,] and universal #emph[Righteousness.] They deny Prodigality, but with worldliness: They separate from the World, but live wholly to Themselves, taking no care to exercise #emph[loving Kindness] in the Earth: or they talk Spiritually, and live Vainly: mention Communion with God, and are every way #emph[conformed] to the World; boasting of Forgiveness of Sin, and never Forgiving others: And with such Considerations do poor Creatures harden their hearts in their #emph[Unregeneracy.]]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. They deceive them in making them believe, that if they can come up to their Condition, it shall be well with them; and so it grows an Easy thing, to have the great Temptation of Repute in Religion to wrestle withal: when they may go far #emph[beyond] them, as to what appears in them, and yet come short of Eternal Life; but of these things, and all the Evils of unmortified walking, afterwards.]]
